  "title": "DataAccessV1dot14",
  "description": "K-05 v1.14, a minor version of the data-access calls (T-1353: T-1352's two rulings and the lead's choice between them, DL-687). It only adds to v1.13 (data-access.v1.13.schema.json, frozen and unchanged, referred to here, which refers on to every earlier version down to v1): every v1.13 definition is here under its own name, by reference, save the four restated: claimOutbox.request, to take the optional sendClass; claimOutbox.exchange, to refer to it and to hold a safety claim's answer to its rule; startSignIn.errors, whose text names the unique keys as migration 0034 names them (CQ-292; no error added or changed); and startSignIn.exchange, to refer to it. So every v1 to v1.13 exchange is a v1.14 exchange. Added: claimOutbox's sendClass, whose only value is safety, allowed only with a named recipient (README item 67): the safety-only claim of a danger line's own wake, which waits for the recipient's lock instead of skipping it and walks only the recipient's open rows of send class safety in commit order, taking each it can claim and passing each it cannot, so no row of another class, and no claim on one, holds a safety line back (RULES 4.12; arch 02 line 111; arch 04 lines 201 and 211; NQ-RT-9). Without the field the claim is v1.13's, unchanged. No state, move, table, column, grant, index or migration is added: the walk's filter reads K-04 v1's outbox_rows.send_class. Not model-facing, so number and length limits are schema rules here. Owner: the architect.",
